ruan SMP: never 'recover' (sheng_sigp_recover) a core the CPU driver parked. ArmCpu parks a secondary that fails its MPIDR or
redistributor check in WFI with interrupts off, after cpu_machine_init set InitState|StartedState; the recovery then clears its
SIGPdisabled and every later cross-call/IPI to it waits forever instead of being skipped. Pairs with ArmCpu/armcpu-park-flag.patch.
Goes after ruan-smp-sigp.patch.

--- a/osfmk/arm/cpu_common.c	2026-11-26 18:38:00.991070567 +0530
+++ b/osfmk/arm/cpu_common.c	2026-11-26 18:38:01.159052633 +0530
@@ -413,10 +413,17 @@
  * random early hangs and UFS root failures under SMP: a wakeup IPI to that core was silently dropped). A core in
  * InitState|StartedState runs and takes interrupts, so the flag is cleared here and the signal sent. Counted in sheng_sigp_recovered. */
 volatile uint32_t sheng_sigp_recovered;
+/* ruan: bit per cpu_number that the CPU driver parked for good (ArmCpu parkCore: WFI, interrupts off). Such a core passed
+ * cpu_machine_init (InitState|StartedState) but never takes an IPI: recovering it would turn a skipped signal into a cross-call or
+ * IPI wait that never ends. */
+volatile uint32_t ruan_cpu_parked;
 bool sheng_sigp_recover(cpu_data_t *target_proc);
 bool
 sheng_sigp_recover(cpu_data_t *target_proc)
 {
+	if (os_atomic_load(&ruan_cpu_parked, relaxed) & (1U << (target_proc->cpu_number & 31))) {
+		return false;
+	}
 	if ((os_atomic_load(&target_proc->cpu_flags, relaxed) & (InitState | StartedState)) != (InitState | StartedState)) {
 		return false;
 	}
